=========================================
PAYMENT RECEIVED
=========================================

Method

postPaymentJournal()

Input

PaymentEntity

Business Rules

Use the payment's bank account as the debit account.

Credit the customer's Accounts Receivable control account.

Journal

Debit

Bank

amountReceived

Credit

Accounts Receivable

allocatedAmount

If the payment contains an unallocated balance, credit the Customer Advances (Customer Credit / Unearned Revenue) liability account for the remaining amount.

Example

Payment Received = 6,000

Allocated = 5,000

Unallocated = 1,000

Journal

Debit Bank                    6,000

Credit Accounts Receivable    5,000

Credit Customer Advances      1,000

=========================================
ADDITIONAL ALLOCATION
=========================================

When an existing unallocated payment is allocated later

move the balance

Debit Customer Advances

Credit Accounts Receivable

Only for the newly allocated amount.

=========================================
REMOVE ALLOCATION
=========================================

If an allocation is removed

Reverse

Debit Accounts Receivable

Credit Customer Advances

Only for the amount removed.

=========================================
REFUND
=========================================

Method

postRefundJournal()

Journal

Debit Accounts Receivable (or Customer Advances if refunding unapplied cash)

Credit Bank

Create reversing journal entries using the existing Journal module.

Do not manually update account balances.

Allow the Journal module to handle posting.

=========================================
CANCEL PAYMENT
=========================================

If the business allows cancellation

Create a reversing journal.

Do not delete journals.

